    "result_text": "All 21 tests pass. The implementation is complete and the suite is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe change adds a stable, shared `householdId` for owners who share a household (same last name at the same address). The `sharesHousehold` opt-in that already suppressed the duplicate-rejection (Cp10) now also results in joiners receiving the same `householdId`, which is returned by `GET /api/owners/{id}`.\n\nDesign choice: I derived `householdId` **deterministically** from the normalized last name + address rather than storing a randomly-generated value. This means any two owners in the same household \u2014 including an owner created earlier without the flag \u2014 compute the identical identifier, which is exactly what \"stable shared identifier\" requires, and it needs no database schema change (mirroring how `displayName`/`initials`/`customerCode` are surfaced).\n\nChanges:\n- **`util/Households.java`** (new) \u2014 single source of truth for household logic: `normalize(...)` (trim, collapse whitespace, lower-case) and `householdId(lastName, address)` returning `HH-<12 upper-case hex of SHA-256>`.\n- **`mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 added a `@Mapping` expression that derives `householdId` on every `OwnerDto` (like `displayName`/`initials`).\n- **`resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 added the read-only `householdId` property to the `Owner` schema so the generated DTO carries the field.\n- **`rest/controller/v1/OwnerRestControllerV1.java`** \u2014 refactored the duplicate-household check to use `Households.normalize`, removing the now-duplicated private helper so matching and id-derivation stay in lockstep.\n\nVerified: `Cp10Tests` (3) and `Cp11Tests` (1) pass, and the full suite is green (21 tests, 0 failures).",
